			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1773322294868,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "CPU Time\n\nCPU time is the amount of time the CPU actively spends\nexecuting code for a single request.\n\nExamples of CPU-heavy work:\n\nJSON parsing\nEncryption/decryption\nImage processing\nSorting large data\nBusiness logic calculations\n\nExample:\n\nIf one request needs 20 ms of CPU time:\nThat means the CPU must work for 20 milliseconds to\nfinish that request.\n\nIf you get 100 requests in one second:\nTotal CPU needed = 100 × 20 ms = 2000 ms of CPU",
			"rawText": "CPU Time\n\nCPU time is the amount of time the CPU actively spends executing code for a single request.\n\nExamples of CPU-heavy work:\n\nJSON parsing\nEncryption/decryption\nImage processing\nSorting large data\nBusiness logic calculations\n\nExample:\n\nIf one request needs 20 ms of CPU time:\nThat means the CPU must work for 20 milliseconds to finish that request.\n\nIf you get 100 requests in one second:\nTotal CPU needed = 100 × 20 ms = 2000 ms of CPU",
			"fontSize": 28,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "middle",
			"containerId": "N94Co0Fp",
			"originalText": "CPU Time\n\nCPU time is the amount of time the CPU actively spends executing code for a single request.\n\nExamples of CPU-heavy work:\n\nJSON parsing\nEncryption/decryption\nImage processing\nSorting large data\nBusiness logic calculations\n\nExample:\n\nIf one request needs 20 ms of CPU time:\nThat means the CPU must work for 20 milliseconds to finish that request.\n\nIf you get 100 requests in one second:\nTotal CPU needed = 100 × 20 ms = 2000 ms of CPU",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
